{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback","id":1517850,"title":"Fall of London feedback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-12T17:46:47-07:00","id":1517850,"title":"Fall of London feedback","content":"Any feedback about Fall of London from those whom have either run it or played thru it? One of my players is suggesting we run thru it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T20:46:36-07:00","id":1517858,"title":"","content":"It's okay.<br /> <br /> Which is really something that I think summarizes it. The write-up of London is pretty good and the premise of the Camarilla's second most important city (after Paris) falling to the Second Inquisition is handled probably about as well as it could be.<br /> <br /> A lot of players are allergic to 5th Edition but this is the least offensive adaptation of the Edition for haters as well as lovers with the exception of the OPP supplements. It takes the &quot;cleansing&quot; of London and makes use of enough lore and background from previous editions that you could use it for V20 without difficulty.<br /> Some general thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. The premise of the Second Inquisition wiping out London's vampires due to the fact Mithras arranged it is basically, the &quot;The Vienna Chantry was an inside job&quot; theory. Mithras' human cult is what gives the SI all the firepower and support it needs to kill every vampire in London and, you know what, it works. It doesn't neuter the vampires of the Camarilla but also explains why they could do it in London but nowhere else.<br /> <br /> 2. However, the game is also a treasure hunt for Voldemort's Horocruxes. It is a VERY D&amp;D-esque premise with you gathering all of Mithras' relics so he can do a ritual to restore himself to being a 4th generation Methusaleh.<br /> <br /> 3. The actual premise can be completely skipped. The game sets you up as Mithras followerer possessed acolytes and that doesn't need to be done. All you need to do is have the PCs asked by<br /> the cult to do the job and have enough threat that they say &quot;yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. The fundamental final choice of the game is the one you should be building up to throughout the game. Do the player characters side with the Camarilla, do they side with Mithras, do they side with the SI, or do they betray everyone?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T08:59:08-07:00","id":1517878,"title":"","content":"I would recommend playing it as it has lots of little subplots that spur other adventures and the fallout of the Camarilla losing such a prized domain to the SI and the return of ancient blood god named Mithras who is back and is in the process of regaining his former power and purging himself of whatever remains of Monty Coven essence in there shared form. All in all I think it was a decent sourcebook, but I like Chicago by Night and Cult of the Blood Gods better myself.<br /> <br /> To be fair I use it as means to flesh out my Malkavian's backstory more as he is from London England from the Victorian Era and what kind of interactions he might have with the major Kindred powers there before he departed for the New World before the eve of the 20th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-14-2023, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:16:41-07:00","id":1517898,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed it very much. It brings a lot of lore into V5, expands a few characters - like Richard de Worde and Lord Camden - that we knew relatively little about, had some enjoyable Memoriam sequences, and gives us a look at the Newburgh Group. The actual plot - find the elements of a McGuffin - is pretty weak, but you can use the book as a resource for your own stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:56:02-07:00","id":1517902,"title":"","content":"It would have been nice if it was about the fall of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T16:37:45-07:00","id":1517905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517902#post1517902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would have been nice if it was about the fall of London.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. It's another example of V5 already having a pre-determined conclusion in mind, so it has an event that might be really interesting to <i>play through</i> happen all offscreen.<br /> <br /> Can't have players active during the Fall of London, no no. They might have ideas of <i>stopping it</i>. Can't let that happen.<br /> <br /> There's that classic bit of writing advice: &quot;If this isn't the most interesting period in your protagonist's life, why aren't you writing about THAT?&quot;. In this case, we're skipping over a full-scale attack on London by government-backed vampire hunters, partially orchestrated by one of the most notable Methuselahs in VtM history. It doesn't matter if the story we got was alright. We're coming in later than we really should, if what you want is to offer gaming groups the most exciting and interesting chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T22:25:25-07:00","id":1517918,"title":"","content":"Effectively, there are a couple of major problems, which are touched upon in previous comments:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This isn't the players' story; this is the story of Mithras and some other notables, in which the player characters participate. This is such a dominant theme in stories and chronicles set within the World of Darkness that the writers don't even notice that's what they are doing. The players should never be observers to the metaplot; the metaplot should be background to stories about the player characters in a chronicle.</li> <li>And, in a stock piece of superhero comic logic, we have characters who are canonically dead returning because the writers like them too much to leave them dead. Lord Camden's death is an important plot point in the <i>Giovanni Chronicles</i>; it's meaningful and poignant because he's actually dead, and that it has some emotional charge. That chapter of the <i>Giovanni Chronicle</i>s is called <i>The Sun Has Set</i>, and do you think, maybe, that this title is a statement of some kind? And then Camden back, and Richard de Worde (formerly dead) and even Mithras himself (pretty dead, and the second edition of <i>A World of Darkness</i> doesn't really justify the way the character is written here), it really robs this world of some consequence.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T22:41:26-07:00","id":1517919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517902#post1517902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would have been nice if it was about the fall of London.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it takes place during the Fallen of London.<br /> <br /> Every day, the Camarilla loses ground and by the end, the place has been almost scoured clean of undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T01:07:12-07:00","id":1517926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517919#post1517919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it takes place during the Fallen of London.<br /> <br /> Every day, the Camarilla loses ground and by the end, the place has been almost scoured clean of undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know.<br /> <br /> Getting involved in that bottom part sounds a lot more interesting than being background dots for mithras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T09:00:56-07:00","id":1517953,"title":"","content":"We are toying with the notion of having some of our crew checking out London after the near total purge of the Kindred and finding what went wrong and try to prevent it our domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T10:47:31-07:00","id":1517959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517953#post1517953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are toying with the notion of having some of our crew checking out London after the near total purge of the Kindred and finding what went wrong and try to prevent it our domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have a 6,000 year old vampire pissed off at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T18:54:13-07:00","id":1517998,"title":"","content":"Can you really say you're playing the &quot;Fall of London&quot; if you're mostly engaging in a fetch quest parallel to the action? Sure, Mithras is orchestrating the whole thing. But it's not really ABOUT London's fall. You, the PCs, certainly don't get any opportunities to affect whether London falls to the SI. Only who ends up taking the place of all the Kindred definitely doomed to die.<br /> <br /> That's the problem. Not the technicality over whether it is or is not happening during the Fall of London. But that you, the PCs, are irrelevant to those proceedings. And are instead engaging in a different plot <i>adjacent</i> to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T22:03:35-07:00","id":1518000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517998#post1517998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you really say you're playing the &quot;Fall of London&quot; if you're mostly engaging in a fetch quest parallel to the action? Sure, Mithras is orchestrating the whole thing. But it's not really ABOUT London's fall. You, the PCs, certainly don't get any opportunities to affect whether London falls to the SI. Only who ends up taking the place of all the Kindred definitely doomed to die.<br /> <br /> That's the problem. Not the technicality over whether it is or is not happening during the Fall of London. But that you, the PCs, are irrelevant to those proceedings. And are instead engaging in a different plot <i>adjacent</i> to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On my end, I suppose it's a question of what exactly you think THE FALL OF LONDON should be about. As well as how much agency the PCs can have in such a situation. For me, the thing I would make clear to my PCs in that situation is that they absolutely cannot have an affect. You can't kill the Hunters off because the cat is out of the bag. WIth the Masquerade broken, there's no victory that can be achieved by force of arms or even one single group of vampire powers. It's the DAYS OF FUTURE PAST scenario with vampires instead of mutants and vampire hunter squads instead of Sentinels.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can beat a squad and should definitely have multiple encounters with the SI during the events but it should feel hunted and desperate.<br /> <br /> In any case, here's my advice for running THE FALL OF LONDON:<br /> <br /> \u200b1. Have the PCs be original PCs and Neonates. They should all be residents of London or people that have an attachment there.<br /> 2. Have Mithras' people contact the PCs early on and offer them vast wealth, power, or influence if they get Mithras' objects of power.<br /> 3. Have the PCs consider simply skipping town and find themselves bound by a mystical force of some kind that prevents them from doing so. This will make London claustrophobic. It might be Blood Sorcery, a geas, or simply Mithras having dominating them and they don't realize it,<br /> 4. Things get worse and worse as the proceeding events happen. It should be only a single week in terms of duration but havens getting blown up, vampire minions being grabbed off the street, and the destruction of clubs as well as more all being events.<br /> 5. It shouldn't be Blade but instead no one entirely knows what's going on. The police are rounding up ghouls, the military are providing checkpoints, and the banks are freezing assets but the actual vampire hunting is done by Mithras cultists/Special Ops/SI/Society of Leopold stuff.<br /> 6. Reward cleverness over &quot;rip them to shreds with Protean 2 and Potence.&quot; Social Disciplines work just as well if not better.<br /> 7. Things should make PCs paranoid like car bombs, helicopters in the air, and an atmosphere of Paranoid. I recommend WATCH_DOGS: LEGION for a good example of a London that has changed dramatically.<br /> 8. Queen Anne will be the Camarilla's side and you might also introduce some honest-to-God Punk Anarchs. Both of these will believe Mithras is behind all of this (or Roger De Camden) over believing humans could ever get their ass in gear to do anything.<br /> 9. Have the finale something where the PCs really can make a big difference. They can finish Mithras off forever, they can betray the Camarilla, or they can soften both up by sending in the SI then killing the survivors or--they can leave AFTER giving Mithras his objects and let Caine sort it out.<br /> 10. Throw in some mini-encounters like discovering a group of Thin Bloods are just giving havesn to the Second Inquisition and pretending to be ghouls or feeding people. Not a smatr play but they all register as alive too.\u200b<br /> 11. When I ran the campaign, I also had the Sabbat attack the city during events and gave a brief reprive as the SI vs, the Sabbat caused things to get completely crazy. The Sabbat ends up losing horribly (not expecting humans who can fight back) but it also shows the old power structures no longer matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T00:55:04-07:00","id":1518009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518000#post1518000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On my end, I suppose it's a question of what exactly you think THE FALL OF LONDON should be about. As well as how much agency the PCs can have in such a situation. For me, the thing I would make clear to my PCs in that situation is that they absolutely cannot have an affect. You can't kill the Hunters off because the cat is out of the bag. WIth the Masquerade broken, there's no victory that can be achieved by force of arms or even one single group of vampire powers. It's the DAYS OF FUTURE PAST scenario with vampires instead of mutants and vampire hunter squads instead of Sentinels.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can beat a squad and should definitely have multiple encounters with the SI during the events but it should feel hunted and desperate.<br /> <br /> In any case, here's my advice for running THE FALL OF LONDON:<br /> <br /> \u200b1. Have the PCs be original PCs and Neonates. They should all be residents of London or people that have an attachment there.<br /> 2. Have Mithras' people contact the PCs early on and offer them vast wealth, power, or influence if they get Mithras' objects of power.<br /> 3. Have the PCs consider simply skipping town and find themselves bound by a mystical force of some kind that prevents them from doing so. This will make London claustrophobic. It might be Blood Sorcery, a geas, or simply Mithras having dominating them and they don't realize it,<br /> 4. Things get worse and worse as the proceeding events happen. It should be only a single week in terms of duration but havens getting blown up, vampire minions being grabbed off the street, and the destruction of clubs as well as more all being events.<br /> 5. It shouldn't be Blade but instead no one entirely knows what's going on. The police are rounding up ghouls, the military are providing checkpoints, and the banks are freezing assets but the actual vampire hunting is done by Mithras cultists/Special Ops/SI/Society of Leopold stuff.<br /> 6. Reward cleverness over &quot;rip them to shreds with Protean 2 and Potence.&quot; Social Disciplines work just as well if not better.<br /> 7. Things should make PCs paranoid like car bombs, helicopters in the air, and an atmosphere of Paranoid. I recommend WATCH_DOGS: LEGION for a good example of a London that has changed dramatically.<br /> 8. Queen Anne will be the Camarilla's side and you might also introduce some honest-to-God Punk Anarchs. Both of these will believe Mithras is behind all of this (or Roger De Camden) over believing humans could ever get their ass in gear to do anything.<br /> 9. Have the finale something where the PCs really can make a big difference. They can finish Mithras off forever, they can betray the Camarilla, or they can soften both up by sending in the SI then killing the survivors or--they can leave AFTER giving Mithras his objects and let Caine sort it out.<br /> 10. Throw in some mini-encounters like discovering a group of Thin Bloods are just giving havesn to the Second Inquisition and pretending to be ghouls or feeding people. Not a smatr play but they all register as alive too.\u200b<br /> 11. When I ran the campaign, I also had the Sabbat attack the city during events and gave a brief reprive as the SI vs, the Sabbat caused things to get completely crazy. The Sabbat ends up losing horribly (not expecting humans who can fight back) but it also shows the old power structures no longer matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be considered a cornucopia of bad storytelling advice. In no particular order:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Why would anyone want to play a game where their characters have no agency. If the decisions of the players have no material affect upon the game, why bother even playing? Again, this is an example of what I was criticising upthread, which is where the players are observers in someone else's story. The metaplot is not so interesting that it's worthwhile anyone's time to come along, and see it upfolding as an observer with no ability to influence anything. There's a reason why &quot;To Grandmother's House&quot; is regularly excoriated as the worst published story in the history of the World of Darkness.</li> <li>Preventing characters from skipping town is a spectacularly bad example of railroading. You want to have characters hanging around because the players want to see how the story will unfold, not because their characters have no choice in the matter.</li> <li>Military providing checkpoints? In London? That's just a painful idea for what should be obvious reasons.</li> <li>If a player has invested in Protean and Potence for their character, it is mean-spirited and ultimately wrong not to allow them to use them.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:57:44-07:00","id":1518045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517959#post1517959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't have a 6,000 year old vampire pissed off at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Mithras was just over the 3,000 plus year mark as his embrace date was 1258 BC or is there another older kindred residing in Great Britain from the older sourcebooks? I only have Fall Of London personally and I've been looking up as much lore I can Mithras rule of London that I can find.<br /> <br /> Also a quick question have any of you gamers used Mithras in any major story arc in any fashion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-15-2023, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:24:27-07:00","id":1518086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518045#post1518045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Mithras was just over the 3,000 plus year mark as his embrace date was 1258 BC or is there another older kindred residing in Great Britain from the older sourcebooks? I only have Fall Of London personally and I've been looking up as much lore I can Mithras rule of London that I can find.<br /> <br /> Also a quick question have any of you gamers used Mithras in any major story arc in any fashion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used him in my Winchester setting as a lurking presence in the background. He never actually appeared in person, but his influence drove several different plot points. I think ancients of his power should be used sparingly and preferably, largely off-stage, lest they overwhelm the other protagonists in the story.<br /> <br /> 3,000 is correct. I'm not aware of any canonical characters who are older. I had a couple in my setting who were also an off-stage presence, intended to counterbalance him.<br /> <br /> London by Night for Victorian vampire has a lot on Mithras' rule. Some of it might be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T15:30:31-07:00","id":1518090,"title":"","content":"Check out Dark Ages British Isles for additional info on Mithras' domain of Avalon. The Victorian Age Vampire novels trilogy also deals with Mithras. Beckett's Jyhad Diary also has a chapter that focuses on Mithras and London. It can act as a prologue to Fall of London or set the story in a different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T13:15:21-07:00","id":1518151,"title":"","content":"Thanks Yab for some of the options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T09:53:01-07:00","id":1518178,"title":"","content":"I was able to find Dark Ages Europe today and focused on the British Isle to get a better picture on what Mithras rule is like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T09:56:35-07:00","id":1518180,"title":"","content":"There is actually a whole official book for Dark Ages about the British Isles. I bought it on DTRPG. It\u2019s pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T10:04:19-07:00","id":1518183,"title":"","content":"That is next on my list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T20:55:30-07:00","id":1518214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518086#post1518086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3,000 is correct. I'm not aware of any canonical characters who are older.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiamat/Lantla from <i>Diablerie Britain</i> is/was roughly 5,000 years old, but she spent pretty much the entire Common Era in torpor in a secret tomb and had little to no influence over the British Isles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:45:59-07:00","id":1518230,"title":"","content":"I would argue that <i>Dark Ages: Europe</i> is actually better for the British Isles than <i>Dark Ages: British Isles</i>. The latter has a lot of flab and filler, and is in desperate need of more focus and better editing.<br /> <br /> (The reader may note from my signature that I am not a disinterested observer in the matter...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T09:43:48-07:00","id":1518362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517905#post1517905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^This. It's another example of V5 already having a pre-determined conclusion in mind, so it has an event that might be really interesting to <i>play through</i> happen all offscreen.<br /> <br /> Can't have players active during the Fall of London, no no. They might have ideas of <i>stopping it</i>. Can't let that happen.<br /> <br /> There's that classic bit of writing advice: &quot;If this isn't the most interesting period in your protagonist's life, why aren't you writing about THAT?&quot;. In this case, we're skipping over a full-scale attack on London by government-backed vampire hunters, partially orchestrated by one of the most notable Methuselahs in VtM history. It doesn't matter if the story we got was alright. We're coming in later than we really should, if what you want is to offer gaming groups the most exciting and interesting chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>sorry to bother, but almost no freaking Chronicle from 2nd edition to 3rd gives any PC any autonomy<br /> It's always &quot;if the PCs don't do it, NPC X will do it either way&quot; or &quot;make the PCs try this, but they willl fail&quot;<br /> <br /> you need only read Transylvania, Giovanni Chronicles, Under the Black Cross, Fountains of Crimson Red, Bitter Crusade.... any of them. The best story supplements, are always By Nights, for they simply set the stage for hooks and stories, and let you do what you want. Pre-determined conclusion was the NAME OF THE GAME for most V4- chronicles. It was so frustrating. V5 chronicles are so much better I can hardly believe (Styx and Bones is not good though, its as much a graphic novel where the PCs witness as the past chronicles)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T10:00:50-07:00","id":1518363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518009#post1518009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could be considered a cornucopia of bad storytelling advice. In no particular order:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Why would anyone want to play a game where their characters have no agency. If the decisions of the players have no material affect upon the game, why bother even playing? Again, this is an example of what I was criticising upthread, which is where the players are observers in someone else's story. The metaplot is not so interesting that it's worthwhile anyone's time to come along, and see it upfolding as an observer with no ability to influence anything. There's a reason why &quot;To Grandmother's House&quot; is regularly excoriated as the worst published story in the history of the World of Darkness.</li> <li>Preventing characters from skipping town is a spectacularly bad example of railroading. You want to have characters hanging around because the players want to see how the story will unfold, not because their characters have no choice in the matter.</li> <li>Military providing checkpoints? In London? That's just a painful idea for what should be obvious reasons.</li> <li>If a player has invested in Protean and Potence for their character, it is mean-spirited and ultimately wrong not to allow them to use them.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think you're supposed to read as &quot;force the Players into it&quot;<br /> if the players don't want to play a story in London, or a story about using brains and not brawn, than they should've asked for something else, or the Storyteller should've explained the chronicles theme and purpose better. <br /> <br /> People play for different reasons, some like a more focused story which branches out here and there depending on their choices. I've tried being way more sandbox for my players, and they weren't interested. Missions with stakes and clear possible objectives where they choose which to cater to, that is what they liked. Fall of London wasn't written to be a &quot;do what you want here in the end of the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was never stated that using Protean or Potence would be deleterious in the post. It is in the book, cuz you know... a really massive human force is crashing down on vampires because the Masquerade has been dramatically breached. So being a little more discreet makes a lot of sense. <br /> <br /> The PCs want to survive and probably leave London, that is what the Chronicle is about. How they do is the story. And for them to do it, they need to involve themselves in the political struggles and the Jyhad machinations of Mithras. And yeah, military checkpoinst is crazy in a fantasy setting, but a death squad invading a luxury penthouse and gunning down all vampires there isn't. London is supposed to feel dangerous, and the vampires should feel hunted. That is why there is a system for SI threat level in the book, which is very nice, for it reacts with the players' actions.<br /> <br /> I find FoL fun and with nice characters, but the main script of gathering relics... yeah, feels a bit... out of place even. Could simply be calling in old favors of Mithras from important London's Kindred or whatever. But it was the first chronicle of the V5 line, and it wasn't so bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T11:27:31-07:00","id":1518365,"title":"","content":"I really liked Fall of London. I thought it was a great Chronicle.<br /> <br /> P: if you\u2019re out there, hi! Thanks for liking my post about the British Isles book \ud83d\ude0a. - T","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 07-20-2023, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:14:51-07:00","id":1518371,"title":"","content":"I didn't read about the fall of London, but from the comments, I understood that there was a mess and they put someone who writes Novels to write a supplement, did I understand the situation correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T11:11:57-07:00","id":1518435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518230#post1518230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that <i>Dark Ages: Europe</i> is actually better for the British Isles than <i>Dark Ages: British Isles</i>. The latter has a lot of flab and filler, and is in desperate need of more focus and better editing.<br /> <br /> (The reader may note from my signature that I am not a disinterested observer in the matter...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rate &quot;England Will Burn&quot; higher than either of the official Dark Ages books. It focuses solely on vampires, which Dark Ages: Britain doesn't, and it contains all the details you'd need to run in a diverse range of domains - including maps, an oft-overlooked but very valuable feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T11:24:58-07:00","id":1518437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518365#post1518365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked Fall of London. I thought it was a great Chronicle.<br /> <br /> P: if you\u2019re out there, hi! Thanks for liking my post about the British Isles book \ud83d\ude0a. - T</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T11:59:50-07:00","id":1518439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518371#post1518371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read about the fall of London, but from the comments, I understood that there was a mess and they put someone who writes Novels to write a supplement, did I understand the situation correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you basically have everything wrong, the book was developed by Matthew Dawkins and written by a number of other freelancers who are also OPP regulars. <br /> <br /> It's not a mess, although this may be more a matter of personal taste: it's a peculiar story, written with a specific cast of characters in mind, where the PCs go raiding relics in a sandboxy way to either help or defeat a Methuselah, while the Inquisition is raiding the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:28:12-07:00","id":1518498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518439#post1518439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you basically have everything wrong, the book was developed by Matthew Dawkins and written by a number of other freelancers who are also OPP regulars.<br /> <br /> It's not a mess, although this may be more a matter of personal taste: it's a peculiar story, written with a specific cast of characters in mind, where the PCs go raiding relics in a sandboxy way to either help or defeat a Methuselah, while the Inquisition is raiding the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawkins was only involved in the very early stages of the book a fact that he has made extremely clear on many occasions and in a number of interviews in order to distance himself from the mess that the book is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:46:17-07:00","id":1518538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518371#post1518371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read about the fall of London, but from the comments, I understood that there was a mess and they put someone who writes Novels to write a supplement, did I understand the situation correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more a toolkit setting where you can either support either faction and Mithras return isn't a sure thing and we have at least 3 different options on how it could end. It's to me a good way to build up good story ideas for our games and as I stated before that I use it as a basis for fleshing out my Malkavian's time in London England during Mithras or Valerius rulership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:27:30-07:00","id":1518547,"title":"","content":"My group decided to play Chicago this time around but I could easily see adapting some Fall of London info for use in a Victorian Age campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T14:39:03-07:00","id":1518570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518498#post1518498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dawkins was only involved in the very early stages of the book a fact that he has made extremely clear on many occasions and in a number of interviews in order to distance himself from the mess that the book is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point me to some of these interviews where he is distancing himself from the book? I'd be interested, as he is still listed as developer along Steffie de Vaan, and she and all the other freelancers involved are people he praises a lot and often works with on other OPP gigs, as far as I know<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_London\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_London</a><br /> <br /> BTW, if I'm not mistaken, at the time he was basically the Wod lead developer for Modiphius","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T19:35:41-07:00","id":1518600,"title":"","content":"I recently listened to an interview he did on 25 Years of VtM podcast. He mentioned that he started developing Fall of London but then handed it off to other writers due to other work commitments. He didn't really keep track of the project then but didn't denigrate the final project at all. I haven't seen/heard any other interviews he did talking about Fall of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T19:49:20-07:00","id":1518602,"title":"","content":"Personally, my issue isn't that Fall of London is bad. It's that it's not what its title implies to be. Instead of being about the Fall of London - where you participate directly in the assault of Camarilla holdings in the city by the Second Inquisition - it's an unrelated matter. Where adventuring in London as a setting is almost an afterthought to the business of assembling plot coupons and bringing Mithras back (or not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T18:38:08-07:00","id":1518799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518602#post1518602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, my issue isn't that Fall of London is bad. It's that it's not what its title implies to be. Instead of being about the Fall of London - where you participate directly in the assault of Camarilla holdings in the city by the Second Inquisition - it's an unrelated matter. Where adventuring in London as a setting is almost an afterthought to the business of assembling plot coupons and bringing Mithras back (or not).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that would be a HUNTER: THE RECKONING book rather than a VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE one. Also, part of the point is the Inquisition isn't really the enemy.<br /> <br /> The player characters have a rare chance to see behind the curtain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T14:57:31-07:00","id":1519050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1518799#post1518799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, that would be a HUNTER: THE RECKONING book rather than a VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE one.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I said &quot;participate directly in the assault of Camarilla holdings&quot;, I meant &quot;on the side of the Camarilla&quot;. Unless you decide to do your own thing. Which is sort of the point. You SHOULD be given more room to involve yourself in the whole &quot;London's Kindred power structures being dismantled by the Inquisition&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, part of the point is the Inquisition isn't really the enemy. </div> </div> </div>This is more a problem with V5/the Second Inquisition as a whole, and less just this adventure.<br /> <br /> Used to be, when you got the attention of hunters, it was Bad, but in a way that created actionable conflict.<br /> <br /> Now, if you caught the attention of hunters, you might as well burn your character sheet, because you're already dead. It's not an enemy to be challenged by, it's a bludgeon to force players into a very narrow play pattern. &quot;Don't engage in BadWrongFun, or the government will come and end the campaign&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The player characters have a rare chance to see behind the curtain. </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't really care what the intent of the adventure was. If you (the writers) center an adventure in a time and place of massive political upheaval, you (the writers) can't complain that people are dissatisfied they aren't allowed to get involved in that.<br /> <br /> You (the writers) are squandering a perfectly good shadow war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T07:08:48-07:00","id":1519108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1517878#post1517878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend playing it as it has lots of little subplots that spur other adventures and the fallout of the Camarilla losing such a prized domain to the SI and the return of ancient blood god named Mithras who is back and is in the process of regaining his former power and purging himself of whatever remains of Monty Coven essence in there shared form. All in all I think it was a decent sourcebook, but I like Chicago by Night and Cult of the Blood Gods better myself.<br /> <br /> To be fair I use it as means to flesh out my Malkavian's backstory more as he is from London England from the Victorian Era and what kind of interactions he might have with the major Kindred powers there before he departed for the New World before the eve of the 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are looking to flesh out that aspect of your character, i really suggest looking into the second and third parts of Giovanni Chronicles, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_II:_Blood_%26_Fire\" target=\"_blank\">Blood &amp; Fire</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_III:_The_Sun_Has_Set\" target=\"_blank\">the Sun Has Set</a>, since considerable chunks of those adventures are set in London (in 1666 and 1848 respectively) and may provide you with a respectable number of NPCs, plotlines and loose threads to weave together with the threadbare basics offered by London by Night or the bits on the city in 1st &amp; 2nd edition World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> (second part of the Sun Has Set takes the PCs to 1882 Egypt, what while quite a move can make for a fun flashpoint or sidetrek of sorts to any ancestors or past acquaintances of your Malkavian's backstory, be they directly connected to the search for the Sargon Fragment or not)<br /> <br /> Other alternate materials to possibly mine for NPCs and fluff tidbits would be Bloody Hearts: Diablerie Britain, Kindred Most Wanted, Dread Names: Red List and BJD, for the references to Tiamat and her descendants the methuselah Gotsdam and his childe the Anathema Dylan Bruce (plus BJD has a chapter on its own on London that can provide for some good complement and contrast to Fall of London).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-29-2023, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:16:29-07:00","id":1519578,"title":"","content":"Speaking again of forgotten characters in previous books, London as described in World of Darkness and Giovanni Chronicles seems to have a history of &quot;high-class diabolist cabals&quot; in the form of the Crimson Bacchanal between 1660s to 1840s at least, that has counted kindred such as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Andre_Mallotte\" target=\"_blank\">Mallotte</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duke_of_Amber\" target=\"_blank\">Duke</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duchess_of_Amber\" target=\"_blank\">Duchess</a> Amber (estranged childer of Mithras - supposedly*),\u200b twins Freia &amp; Frigga (Sabbat infiltrators, childer of notorious insane vicissitude &amp; brainwashing master known as the Sculptor) and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Anne</a> among its ranks through the ages, while in contemporary times (or at least the '90s) many were the tales of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Count_Zaroff\" target=\"_blank\">Count Zaroff</a>'s Hunt Club.<br /> <br /> Also the Foundlings coterie and specially <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tobias_Leveler\" target=\"_blank\">Tobias</a> with his ties to the leveler movement in the 1600s, if surviving the events of Blood &amp; Fire, could evolve into a foundation for the Anarch movement or at least one of its factions within the city.<br /> <br /> [In fact when a friend STed the Sun has Set, along with the Ambers as allies/patrons of Lady Anne, &quot;Mr. Leveler&quot; also made a comeback as a 7th gen local anarch leader, somewhere between <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Juggler\" target=\"_blank\">Juggler</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Stephen_Lenoir\" target=\"_blank\">Lenoir</a> in behaviour, with the &quot;Foundlings&quot; as his extended coterie/anarch faction/pupils plus some stealth contacts among the Tremere through a few &quot;strays&quot; from failed intrigues on London he rescued through the ages, including acquaintance with Rose Chandler, that by 1848 also happened to be an archon and pupil of one of the PCs, for something of a subplot/monkeywrench in the main plot]<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Sun has Set has a good part of its pagecount dedicated to a story arc in 1848 London that could serve as a very good companion piece for London by Night in scenery and cast, with a score of NPCs such as Toreador Hortense Holden, his childe Victoria Ash**, Gangrel Alice Seymour, the Dunlops, lady Astor of the Lasombra, Streck's pack and others i forget.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The Ambers embrace date of 701 would actually be <b><i>right in the middle of one of Mithras torpor periods</i></b>, meaning they can't be his childer (unless he found some way to embrace kindred while asleep, who knows). Possible alternate explanations are their being childer of another Ventrue 4th gen (Tiamat?) that the Sun-God later brainwashed &amp; adopted for reasons his own, OR they are the childer of one of his own estranged childer (like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cretheus\" target=\"_blank\">Cret</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Marcus_Verus\" target=\"_blank\">Verus</a>) who joined his ranks and later rose to 5th gen through diablerie.<br /> <br /> **<b>Not</b> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Victoria_Ash\" target=\"_blank\">that one</a>\u200b, just an homonym - though considering they have the same name, clan and generation, not to mention the better known Victoria has <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Regina_Blake\" target=\"_blank\">a childe</a> amidst London's court, making them into one and the same (falsifying her descendance for who knows what motives) would be all too simple. Or have them both for a bit of confusion, humor and petty rivalries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T12:10:39-07:00","id":1519976,"title":"","content":"I wonder what happened to some of Mithras childer in the later ages and if they survived to the modern nights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T22:11:24-07:00","id":1520014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1519976#post1519976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what happened to some of Mithras childer in the later ages and if they survived to the modern nights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mithras_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">his profile</a> in the wiki does have a &quot;childer&quot; header with links to their own, a definite start. But to summarize things:<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cretheus\" target=\"_blank\">Cretheus</a> since the middle ages has become a leading member of the Inconnu.<br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Marcus_Verus\" target=\"_blank\">Marcus Verus</a> apparently remained as prince of Chester well into modern times, at least until his exposure as a member of Gehenna Cults such as the<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Royal_Order_of_Edenic_Groundskeepers\" target=\"_blank\">Royal Order of Edenic Groundskeepers</a> or the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tal%27mahe%27Ra\" target=\"_blank\">Tal'Mahe'Ra</a>, if not both. Some rumors even speak of him in Tunisia having a battle with Christof Romuald<br /> near the supposed resting place of the Brujah Antediluvian...<br /> - The <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duke_of_Amber\" target=\"_blank\">Amber</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Duchess_of_Amber\" target=\"_blank\">couple</a>, if memory tricks me not, were still part of London's court in 1848 (as of the Sun Has Set) and are cited as major supporters of Lady Anne,<br /> possibly key in her replacement of her sire Valerius (an act possibly sweet for them, since Valerius was the one who replaced them as Mithras' right hand<br /> much as they succeeded Camden).<br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Geraint\" target=\"_blank\">Geraint</a>, is something of a footnote and enigma, even in the DA book that first cited him, might be said.<br /> \u200b<br /> Any others are up to homebrewing of one's own wicked imagination (though one could say that Geraint exist as a conveniently blank piece of canon for STs to slot whatever they might need).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-08-2023, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:47:18-07:00","id":1520126,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the links that you gave out and I'm somewhat amazed that Mithras was such a prolific sire at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T10:09:05-07:00","id":1520134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1520126#post1520126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the links that you gave out and I'm somewhat amazed that Mithras was such a prolific sire at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he's a 3000+ years vampire, plenty of time to embrace here and there.<br /> That said, as i previously pointed out, the Ambers are a <b>very</b> sketchy case in that they should <b>not</b> be truly Mithras' childer based on the embrace date.<br /> If it's not handwaved (as the continuity hiccup it is) it's hard to ignore that something bizarre is being covered up by that claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T16:17:24-07:00","id":1520157,"title":"","content":"I certainly thought out only Michael was a prolific sire of childer in the setting Baaldam and that the others were more like Montano, Dracon, and others very choosy about whom they chose as childer themselves and a dude who sees itself as a god would fall in that camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T18:32:43-08:00","id":1525490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1520157#post1520157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly thought out only Michael was a prolific sire of childer in the setting Baaldam and that the others were more like Montano, Dracon, and others very choosy about whom they chose as childer themselves and a dude who sees itself as a god would fall in that camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Well, Mithras supposedly embraced 5 kindred (3 if the Ambers' lineage is actually falsified) in about 1131 years, while Michael produced <b><i>at least</i></b> 7 childer in around 685 years. May not seem like much in the end, but it's a huge difference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":114